FT                   /note="Domain:cl26133:NRDD Anaerobic
FT                   ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase. This model
FT                   represents the oxygen-sensitive (anaerobic, class III)
FT                   ribonucleotide reductase. The mechanism of the enzyme
FT                   involves a glycine-centered radical, a C-terminal zinc
FT                   binding site, and a set of conserved active site cysteines
FT                   and asparagines. This enzyme requires an activating
FT                   component, NrdG, a radical-SAM domain containing enzyme
FT                   (TIGR02491). Together the two form an alpha-2/beta-2
FT                   heterodimer. [Purines, pyrimidines, nucleosides, and
FT                   nucleotides, 2'-Deoxyribonucleotide metabolism]
