FT                   phosphonate, periplasmic substrate-binding protein. Members
FT                   of this family ABC transporter periplasmic binding proteins
FT                   and represent one clade within a larger family that
FT                   includes phosphate, phosphite, and phosphonate
FT                   transporters. All members of the seed alignment occur near
FT                   a gene for SelD, the selenium-activating protein needed to
FT                   make selenocysteine or selenouridine. Context therefore
FT                   suggests members should be able to transport selenate,
FT                   although transporting other substrates as well (e.g.
FT                   phosphonates) is possible. This model has no overlap with
