FT                   Eval:2.0e-104]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl26002:TPR_11 TPR repeat. The
FT                   Tetratricopeptide repeat (TPR) typically contains 34 amino
FT                   acids and is found in a variety of organisms including
FT                   bacteria, cyanobacteria, yeast, fungi, plants, and humans.
FT                   It is present in a variety of proteins including those
FT                   involved in chaperone, cell-cycle, transcription, and
FT                   protein transport complexes. The number of TPR motifs
FT                   varies among proteins. Those containing 5-6 tandem repeats
FT                   generate a right-handed helical structure with an
FT                   amphipathic channel that is thought to accommodate an
FT                   alpha-helix of a target protein. It has been proposed that
FT                   TPR proteins preferentially interact with WD-40 repeat
FT                   proteins, but in many instances several TPR-proteins seem
FT                   to aggregate to multi-protein complexes. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:10-236, Eval:1.2e-16, score:74.0]"
FT                   /note="MGA_763"
