FT                   /note="Domain:cl09141:ACT ACT domains are commonly involved
FT                   in specifically binding an amino acid or other small ligand
FT                   leading to regulation of the enzyme. The ACT domain is a
FT                   structural motif of 70-90 amino acids that functions in the
FT                   control of metabolism, solute transport and signal
FT                   transduction. They are thus found in a variety of different
FT                   proteins in a variety of different arrangements. In
FT                   mammalian phenylalanine hydroxylase the domain forms no
FT                   contacts but promotes an allosteric effect despite the
FT                   apparent lack of ligand binding. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:2-77, Eval:7.1e-23, score:89.3]"
