FT                   /note="Domain:cl21515:GAF GAF domain. SpoVT_C is the
FT                   C-terminal part of the stage V sporulation protein T, a
FT                   transcription factor involved in endospore formation in
FT                   Gram-positive bacteria such as Bacillus subtilis.
FT                   Sporulation is induced by conditions of environmental
FT                   stress to protect the genome. SpoVT behaves as a tetramer
FT                   that shows an overall significant distortion mediated by
FT                   electrostatic interactions. Two monomers dimerize via the
FT                   highly charged N-terminal AbrB-like domains, family
FT                   pfam04014, to form swapped-hairpin beta-barrels. These
FT                   asymmetric dimers then form tetramers through the formation
FT                   of mixed helix bundles between their C-terminal domains.
FT                   The C-termini themselves fold as GAF (cGMP-specific and
FT                   cGMP-stimulated phosphodiesterases, Anabaena adenylate
FT                   cyclases, and Escherichia coli FhlA) domains. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:25-237, Eval:2.0e-71, score:214.9]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1265"
