FT                   /note="Domain:cl01115:BMFP Membrane fusogenic activity.
FT                   BMFP consists of two structural domains, a coiled-coil
FT                   C-terminal domain via which the protein self-associates as
FT                   a trimer, and an N-terminal domain disordered at neutral pH
FT                   but adopting an amphipathic alpha-helical structure in the
FT                   presence of phospholipid vesicles, high ionic strength,
FT                   acidic pH or SDS. BMFP interacts with phospholipid vesicles
FT                   though the predicted amphipathic alpha-helix induced in the
FT                   N-terminal half of the protein and promotes aggregation and
FT                   fusion of vesicles in vitro. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-92,
FT                   Eval:1.0e-23, score:84.1]"
