FT                   /note="Domain:cl21526:TolB_N TolB amino-terminal domain.
FT                   This is a family of Gram-negative bacterial outer membrane
FT                   lipoproteins. LpoB is required for the function of the
FT                   major peptidoglycan synthase enzyme PBP1B. It interacts
FT                   with PBP1B protein via the UvrB-like non-catalytic domain
FT                   on that protein. LpoB has a 54-aa-long flexible N-terminal
FT                   stretch followed by a globular domain with similarity to
FT                   the N-terminal domain of the prevalent periplasmic protein
FT                   TolB. The long, flexible N-terminal region of LpoB enables
FT                   it to span the periplasm and reach its docking site in
FT                   PBP1B. Peptidoglycan is the essential polymer within the
FT                   sacculus that surrounds the cytoplasmic membrane of
FT                   bacteria. [Superfamily, Aligned:4-193, Eval:3.4e-24,
FT                   score:91.9]"
