FT                   /note="Domain:cl14607:OPT OPT oligopeptide transporter
FT                   protein. This protein represents a small family of integral
FT                   membrane proteins from Gram-negative bacteria, a
FT                   Gram-positive bacteria, and an archaeal species. Members of
FT                   this family contain 15 to 18 GES predicted transmembrane
FT                   regions, and this family has extensive homology to a family
FT                   of yeast tetrapeptide transporters, including isp4
FT                   (Schizosaccharomyces pombe) and Opt1 (Candida albicans).
FT                   EspB, an apparent equivalog from Myxococcus xanthus, shares
FT                   an operon with a two component system regulatory protein,
FT                   and is required for the normal timing of sporulation after
FT                   the aggregation of cells. This is consistent with a role in
FT                   transporting oligopeptides as signals across the membrane.
FT                   [Transport and binding proteins, Amino acids, peptides and
FT                   amines] [Superfamily, Aligned:14-567, Eval:1.5e-31,
FT                   score:126.3]"
