FT                   /note="COG:COG0366:AmyA Glycosidase [Category:G,
FT                   Aligned:20-533, Eval:9.8e-132, score:407.5]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl23844:Ble Predicted trehalose synthase
FT                   [Carbohydrate transport and metabolism]. Three pathways for
FT                   the biosynthesis of trehalose, an osmoprotectant that in
FT                   some species is also a precursor of certain cell wall
FT                   glycolipids. Trehalose synthase, TreS, can interconvert
FT                   maltose and trehalose, but while the equilibrium may favor
FT                   trehalose, physiological concentrations of trehalose may be
FT                   much greater than that of maltose and TreS may act largely
FT                   in its degradation. This model describes a domain found
FT                   only as a C-terminal fusion to TreS proteins. The most
FT                   closely related proteins outside this family, Pep2 of
FT                   Streptomyces coelicolor and Mak1 of Actinoplanes
FT                   missouriensis, have known maltokinase activity. We suggest
FT                   this domain acts as a maltokinase and helps drive
FT                   conversion of trehalose to maltose. [Energy metabolism,
FT                   Biosynthesis and degradation of polysaccharides]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:635-1101, Eval:9.3e-94, score:303.8]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1704"
