FT                   /note="Domain:cl25951:NAD_binding_11 NAD-binding of
FT                   NADP-dependent 3-hydroxyisobutyrate dehydrogenase. This
FT                   family resembles a larger family (gnd) of bacterial and
FT                   eukaryotic 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenases but differs
FT                   from it by a deep split in a UPGMA similarity clustering
FT                   tree and the lack of a central region of about 140
FT                   residues. Among complete genomes, it is found is found in
FT                   Bacillus subtilis and Mycobacterium tuberculosis, both of
FT                   which also contain gnd, and in Aquifex aeolicus. The
FT                   protein from Methylobacillus flagellatus KT has been
FT                   characterized as a decarboxylating 6-phosphogluconate
FT                   dehydrogenase as part of an unusual formaldehyde oxidation
FT                   cycle. In some sequenced organisms members of this family
FT                   are the sole 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase present and
FT                   are probably active in the pentose phosphate cycle. [Energy
FT                   metabolism, Pentose phosphate pathway] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:1-324, Eval:1.8e-157, score:439.9]"
