FT                   /note="Domain:cl01544:Bestrophin Bestrophin, RFP-TM,
FT                   chloride channel. Bestrophin is a 68-kDa basolateral plasma
FT                   membrane protein expressed in retinal pigment epithelial
FT                   cells (RPE). It is encoded by the VMD2 gene, which is
FT                   mutated in Best macular dystrophy, a disease characterized
FT                   by a depressed light peak in the electrooculogram. VMD2
FT                   encodes a 585-amino acid protein with an approximate mass
FT                   of 68 kDa which has been designated bestrophin. Bestrophin
FT                   shares homology with the Caenorhabditis elegans RFP gene
FT                   family, named for the presence of a conserved arginine (R),
FT                   phenylalanine (F), proline (P), amino acid sequence motif.
FT                   Bestrophin is a plasma membrane protein, localized to the
FT                   basolateral surface of RPE cells consistent with a role for
FT                   bestrophin in the generation or regulation of the EOG light
FT                   peak. Bestrophin and other RFP family members represent a
FT                   new class of chloride channels, indicating a direct role
FT                   for bestrophin in generating the light peak. The VMD2 gene
FT                   underlying Best disease was shown to represent the first
FT                   human member of the RFP-TM protein family. More than 97% of
FT                   the disease-causing mutations are located in the N-terminal
FT                   RFP-TM domain implying important functional properties. The
FT                   bestrophins are four-pass transmembrane chloride-channel
FT                   proteins, and the RFP-TM or bestrophin domain extends from
FT                   the N-terminus through approximately 350 amino acids and
FT                   contains all of the TM domains as well as nearly all
FT                   reported disease causing mutations. Interestingly, the RFP
FT                   motif is not conserved evolutionarily back beyond Metazoa,
FT                   neither is it in plant members. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:23-298, Eval:8.6e-54, score:175.3]"
FT                   /note="MGA_2520"
