FT                   /note="Domain:cl22877:Autotransporter Autotransporter
FT                   beta-domain. A number of Gram-negative bacterial proteins,
FT                   mostly found in pathogens and associated with virulence,
FT                   contain a conserved C-terminal domain that integrates into
FT                   the outer membrane and enables the N-terminal region to be
FT                   delivered across the membrane. This C-terminal
FT                   autotransporter domain is about 400 amino acids in length
FT                   and includes the aromatic amino acid-rich OMP signal,
FT                   typically ending with a Phe or Trp residue, at the extreme
FT                   C-terminus. [Protein fate, Protein and peptide secretion
