FT                   s_cov:100.0%, Eval:6.5e-103]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl21614:YkuD L,D-transpeptidase catalytic
FT                   domain. This family of proteins are found in a range of
FT                   bacteria. It has been shown that this domain can act as an
FT                   L,D-transpeptidase that gives rise to an alternative
FT                   pathway for peptidoglycan cross-linking. This gives
FT                   bacteria resistance to beta-lactam antibiotics that inhibit
FT                   PBPs which usually carry out the cross-linking reaction.
FT                   The conserved region contains a conserved histidine and
FT                   cysteine, with the cysteine thought to be an active site
FT                   residue. Several members of this family contain
FT                   peptidoglycan binding domains. The molecular structure of
FT                   YkuD protein shows this domain has a novel tertiary fold
FT                   consisting of a beta-sandwich with two mixed sheets, one
FT                   containing five strands and the other, six strands. The two
FT                   beta-sheets form a cradle capped by an alpha-helix. This
FT                   family was formerly called the ErfK/YbiS/YcfS/YnhG family,
FT                   but is now named after the first protein of known
FT                   structure. [Superfamily, Aligned:48-187, Eval:2.9e-48,
FT                   score:156.4, C-term missing]"
FT                   /note="MGA_2616"
