FT                   /note="Domain:cl28008:PaaK Phenylacetate-coenzyme A ligase
FT                   PaaK, adenylate-forming domain family [Coenzyme transport
FT                   and metabolism]. Members of this family form a distinct
FT                   clade within a larger family of proteins that also includes
FT                   coenzyme F390 synthetase, an enzyme known in
FT                   Methanobacterium thermoautotrophicum and a few other
FT                   methanogenic archaea. That enzyme adenylates coenzyme F420
FT                   to F390, a reversible process, during oxygen stress. Other
FT                   informative homologies include domains of the non-ribosomal
FT                   peptide synthetases involved in activation by adenylation.
FT                   The family defined by this model is likely to be of an
FT                   adenylate-forming enzyme related to but distinct from
FT                   coenzyme F390 synthetase. [Superfamily, Aligned:63-358,
FT                   Eval:2.9e-18, score:83.1, N-term missing]"
