FT                   /note="Domain:cl19847:DUF1285 Protein of unknown function
FT                   (DUF1285). This family consists of several hypothetical
FT                   bacterial proteins of around 200 residues in length. The
FT                   function of this family is unknown. The structures revealed
FT                   a conserved core with domain duplication and a superficial
FT                   similarity of the C-terminal domain to pleckstrin
FT                   homology-like folds. The conservation of the domain-
FT                   interface indicates a potential binding site that is likely
FT                   to involve a nucleotide-based ligand, with genome-context
FT                   and gene-fusion analyses additionally supporting a role for
FT                   this family in signal transduction, possibly during
FT                   oxidative stress. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-183,
