FT                   /note="WP_005614684.1 amidinotransferase (Pseudomonas)
FT                   [pid:88.8%, q_cov:100.0%, s_cov:100.0%, Eval:9.2e-201]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl19186:Amidinotransf Amidinotransferase.
FT                   Peptidyl-arginine deiminase (PAD) enzymes catalyze the
FT                   deimination of the guanidino group from carboxy-terminal
FT                   arginine residues of various peptides to produce ammonia.
FT                   PAD from Porphyromonas gingivalis (PPAD) appears to be
FT                   evolutionarily unrelated to mammalian PAD (pfam03068),
FT                   which is a metalloenzyme. PPAD is thought to belong to the
FT                   same superfamily as aminotransferase and arginine
FT                   deiminase, and to form an alpha/beta propeller structure.
FT                   This family has previously been named PPADH (Porphyromonas
FT                   peptidyl-arginine deiminase homologs). The predicted
FT                   catalytic residues in PPAD are Asp130, Asp187, His236,
FT                   Asp238 and Cys351. These are absolutely conserved with the
FT                   exception of Asp187 which is absent in two family members.
FT                   PPAD is also able to catalyze the deimination of free
FT                   L-arginine, but has primarily peptidyl-arginine
FT                   specificity. It may have a FMN cofactor. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:61-354, Eval:3.4e-09, score:54.3]"
FT                   /note="MGA_3356"
