FT                   /note="Domain:cl28320:FlgK Flagellar hook-associated
FT                   protein FlgK [Cell motility]. The flagellar hook-associated
FT                   protein FlgK of bacterial flagella has conserved N- and
FT                   C-terminal domains. The central region is highly variable
FT                   in length and sequence, and often contains substantial runs
FT                   of low-complexity sequence. This model is built from an
FT                   alignment of FlgK sequences with the central region
FT                   excised. Note that several other proteins of the flagellar
FT                   apparatus also are homologous in the N- and C-terminal
FT                   regions to FlgK, but are excluded from this model.
