FT                   /note="Domain:cl10012:DnaQ_like_exo DnaQ-like (or DEDD)
FT                   3&apos;-5&apos; exonuclease domain superfamily. This is a
FT                   highly divergent 3' exoribonuclease family. The proteins
FT                   constitute a typical RNase fold, where the active site
FT                   residues form a magnesium catalytic centre. The protein of
FT                   the solved structure readily cleaves 3### overhangs in a
FT                   time-dependent manner. It is similar to DEDD-type RNases
FT                   and is an unusual ATP-binding protein that binds ATP and
FT                   dATP. It forms a dimer in solution and both protomers in
