FT                   subunit PhnI (Pseudomonas syringae) [pid:93.9%,
FT                   q_cov:100.0%, s_cov:100.0%, Eval:5.0e-191]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl01456:PhnI Bacterial phosphonate metabolism
FT                   protein (PhnI). This family consists of several
FT                   Proteobacterial phosphonate metabolism protein (PhnI)
FT                   sequences. Bacteria that use phosphonates as a phosphorus
FT                   source must be able to break the stable carbon-phosphorus
FT                   bond. In Escherichia coli phosphonates are broken down by a
FT                   C-P lyase that has a broad substrate specificity. The genes
FT                   for phosphonate uptake and degradation in E. coli are
FT                   organised in an operon of 14 genes, named phnC to phnP.
FT                   Three gene products (PhnC, PhnD and PhnE) comprise a
FT                   binding protein-dependent phosphonate transporter, which
FT                   also transports phosphate, phosphite, and certain phosphate
FT                   esters such as phosphoserine; two gene products (PhnF and
FT                   PhnO) may have a role in gene regulation; and nine gene
FT                   products (PhnG, PhnH, PhnI, PhnJ, PhnK, PhnL, PhnM, PhnN,
FT                   and PhnP) probably comprise a membrane-associated C-P lyase
FT                   enzyme complex. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-349, Eval:0.0e+00,
FT                   score:636.0]"
FT                   /note="MGA_3651"
