FT                   [pid:86.8%, q_cov:99.0%, s_cov:99.8%, Eval:2.2e-246]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl00256:CheW_like N/A. CheW proteins are part
FT                   of the chemotaxis signaling mechanism in bacteria. CheW
FT                   interacts with the methyl accepting chemotaxis proteins
FT                   (MCPs) and relays signals to CheY, which affects flageller
FT                   rotation. This family includes CheW and other related
FT                   proteins that are involved in chemotaxis. The CheW-like
