FT                   /note="Domain:cl21707:Phage_holin_3_6 Putative
FT                   Actinobacterial Holin-X, holin superfamily III.
FT                   Phage_holin_3_6 is a family of small hydrophobic proteins
FT                   with two or three transmembrane domains of the Hol-X
FT                   family. Holin proteins are produced by double-stranded DNA
FT                   bacteriophages that use an endolysin-holin strategy to
FT                   achieve lysis of their hosts. The endolysins are
FT                   peptidoglycan-degrading enzymes that are usually
FT                   accumulated in the cytosol until access to the cell wall
FT                   substrate is provided by the holin membrane lesion.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:15-130, Eval:1.3e-28, score:98.7]"
