FT                   /note="Domain:cl26602:SunT ABC-type bacteriocin/lantibiotic
FT                   exporters, contain an N-terminal double-glycine peptidase
FT                   domain  [Defense mechanisms]. Members of this protein
FT                   family are ABC transporter ATP-binding subunits, part of a
FT                   three-gene putative bacteriocin transport operon. The other
FT                   subunits include another ATP-binding subunit (TIGR03796),
FT                   which has an N-terminal leader sequence cleavage domain,
FT                   and an HlyD homolog (TIGR03794). In a number of genomes,
FT                   members of protein families related to nitrile hydratase
FT                   alpha subunit or to nif11 have undergone paralogous family
FT                   expansions, with members possessing a putative bacteriocin
FT                   cleavage region ending with a classic Gly-Gly motif. Those
FT                   sets of putative bacteriocins, members of this protein
FT                   family and its partners TIGR03794 and TIGR03796, and
FT                   cyclodehydratase/docking scaffold fusion proteins of
FT                   thiazole/oxazole biosynthesis frequently show correlated
FT                   species distribution and co-clustering within many of those
FT                   genomes. [Transport and binding proteins, Amino acids,
FT                   peptides and amines, Cellular processes, Biosynthesis of
FT                   natural products] [Superfamily, Aligned:10-554,
FT                   Eval:0.0e+00, score:555.2]"
