FT                   N-terminal domain-containing protein (Pseudomonas)
FT                   [pid:91.6%, q_cov:99.2%, s_cov:99.2%, Eval:1.4e-188]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl26137:HSDR_N Type I restriction enzyme R
FT                   protein N terminus (HSDR_N). This family consists of a
FT                   number of N terminal regions found in type I restriction
FT                   enzyme R (HSDR) proteins. Restriction and modification
FT                   (R/M) systems are found in a wide variety of prokaryotes
FT                   and are thought to protect the host bacterium from the
FT                   uptake of foreign DNA. Type I restriction and modification
FT                   systems are encoded by three genes: hsdR, hsdM, and hsdS.
FT                   The three polypeptides, HsdR, HsdM, and HsdS, often
FT                   assemble to give an enzyme (R2M2S1) that modifies
FT                   hemimethylated DNA and restricts unmethylated DNA.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:1-359, Eval:7.4e-142, score:404.2]"
FT                   /note="MGA_4223"
