FT                   /note="Domain:cl18957:TerD_like Uncharacterized proteins
FT                   involved in stress response, similar to tellurium
FT                   resistance terD. The TerD domain is found in TerD family
FT                   proteins that include the paralogous TerD, TerA, TerE, TerF
FT                   and TerZ proteins It is found in a stress response operon
FT                   with TerB and TerC. TerD has a maximum of two
FT                   calcium-binding sites depending on the conservation of
FT                   aspartates. It has various fusions to nuclease domains, RNA
FT                   binding domains, ubiquitin related domains, and metal
FT                   binding domains. The ter gene products lie at the centre of
FT                   membrane-linked metal recognition complexes with regulatory
FT                   ramifications encompassing phosphorylation-dependent signal
FT                   transduction, RNA-dependent regulation, biosynthesis of
FT                   nucleoside-like metabolites and DNA processing linked to
FT                   novel pathways. [Superfamily, Aligned:64-159, Eval:1.7e-08,
