FT                   /note="Domain:cl28312:UvrD Superfamily I DNA or RNA
FT                   helicase [Replication, recombination and repair]. AddAB,
FT                   also called RexAB, substitutes for RecBCD in several
FT                   bacterial lineages. These DNA recombination proteins act
FT                   before synapse and are particularly important for DNA
FT                   repair of double-stranded breaks by homologous
FT                   recombination. The term AddAB is used broadly, with AddA
FT                   homologous between the Firmicutes (as modeled here) and the
FT                   alphaproteobacteria, while the partner AddB proteins show
