FT                   /note="Domain:cl26823:N_methyl Prokaryotic N-terminal
FT                   methylation motif. This model describes many but not all
FT                   examples of the N-terminal region of bacterial proteins
FT                   that resemble type IV pilins at their N-terminus, with a
FT                   cleavage site G^FxxxE followed by a hydrophobic stretch.
FT                   The new N-terminal residue, usually Phe, is methylated.
FT                   Separate domains of the prepilin peptidase appear
FT                   responsible for cleavage and methylation. Proteins with
FT                   this N-terminal region include type IV pilins and other
FT                   components of pilus biogenesis, competence proteins, and
FT                   type II secretion proteins. Typically several proteins in a
FT                   single operon have this N-terminal domain. The N-terminal
FT                   cleavage and methylation site is described by PROSITE motif
FT                   PS00409 as
FT                   [KRHEQSTAG]-G-[FYLIVM]-[ST]-[LT]-[LIVP]-E-[LIVMFWSTAG](14).
FT                   [Cell envelope, Surface structures, Protein fate, Protein
FT                   and peptide secretion and trafficking] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:2-157, Eval:1.4e-21, score:83.3]"
