FT                   /note="Domain:cl28330:XerC Integrase [Replication,
FT                   recombination and repair, Mobilome: prophages,
FT                   transposons]. The phage integrase family describes a number
FT                   of recombinases with tyrosine active sites that transiently
FT                   bind covalently to DNA. Many are associated with mobile DNA
FT                   elements, including phage, transposons, and phase variation
FT                   loci. This model represents XerD, one of two closely
FT                   related chromosomal proteins along with XerC (TIGR02224).
FT                   XerC and XerD are site-specific recombinases which help
FT                   resolve chromosome dimers to monomers for cell division
FT                   after DNA replication. In species with a large chromosome
FT                   and with homologs of XerD on other replicons, the
FT                   chomosomal copy was preferred for building this model. This
FT                   model does not detect all XerD, as some apparent XerD
FT                   examples score below the trusted and noise cutoff scores.
FT                   XerC and XerD interact with cell division protein FtsK.
FT                   [DNA metabolism, DNA replication, recombination, and
FT                   repair] [Superfamily, Aligned:41-303, Eval:1.6e-44,
FT                   score:151.2]"
FT                   /note="MGA_4984"
